instruction:
You are fixing a bug in the Go repository checked out at /echo (labstack/echo v4). Do NOT touch any *_test.go file, do NOT add new files, and make no changes outside /echo/middleware/proxy.go.

BUG: The proxy middleware panics when the configured balancer has no targets. `randomBalancer.Next` calls `b.random.Intn(len(b.targets))` and `roundRobinBalancer.Next` computes `b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))`; with zero targets these panic (invalid argument to Intn / integer divide by zero). Expected behaviour: with no targets the middleware must not panic and must respond with HTTP 503 Service Unavailable (echo.ErrServiceUnavailable).

APPLY EXACTLY THESE EDITS to /echo/middleware/proxy.go:

1) Replace the body of `func (b *randomBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget` so it becomes:

func (b *randomBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget {
	if b.random == nil {
		b.random = rand.New(rand.NewSource(int64(time.Now().Nanosecond())))
	}
	b.mutex.RLock()
	defer b.mutex.RUnlock()
	if len(b.targets) == 0 {
		return nil
	}
	return b.targets[b.random.Intn(len(b.targets))]
}

2) Replace the body of `func (b *roundRobinBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget` so it becomes:

func (b *roundRobinBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget {
	if len(b.targets) == 0 {
		return nil
	}
	b.i = b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))
	t := b.targets[b.i]
	atomic.AddUint32(&b.i, 1)
	return t
}

3) In `ProxyWithConfig`'s returned handler, right after `tgt := config.Balancer.Next(c)` insert a nil check so the code reads:

			tgt := config.Balancer.Next(c)
			if tgt == nil {
				return echo.ErrServiceUnavailable
			}
			c.Set(config.ContextKey, tgt)

Keep gofmt formatting (run `cd /echo && gofmt -l middleware/proxy.go` and fix if it prints the file).

VERIFY (run these and report verbatim output):
- `cd /echo && go build ./... && go vet ./middleware/`
- `cd /echo && go test ./middleware/ -run 'TestProxy' -v 2>&1 | tail -60`
- `cd /echo && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -40`
- Write a TEMPORARY test file /echo/middleware/zz_notargets_tmp_test.go containing a package middleware test named TestZZNoTargetsTmp that: creates `echo.New()`, uses `NewRoundRobinBalancer([]*ProxyTarget{})` via `e.Use(Proxy(balancer))`, sends `httptest.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, "/", nil)` through `e.ServeHTTP(rec, req)` and asserts `rec.Code == http.StatusServiceUnavailable`; then a second sub-case doing the same with `NewRandomBalancer(nil)` and asserting 503. Run `cd /echo && go test ./middleware/ -run TestZZNoTargetsTmp -v`, report the output, then DELETE that temporary file (`rm /echo/middleware/zz_notargets_tmp_test.go`) and confirm `git status --porcelain` shows only middleware/proxy.go modified.

Report: the exact diff (`cd /echo && git diff`), all command outputs, and whether everything passed. If any pre-existing test fails, report which one and its output.

Fix a bug in /echo/context.go (Go, labstack/echo). Only edit /echo/context.go; do NOT touch any *_test.go file permanently (temporary test files must be deleted before you finish).

BUG: `func (c *context) Scheme() string` (around line 252) returns whatever value is in the X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Forwarded-Protocol / X-Url-Scheme headers even when the value is not a valid scheme. Expected: invalid header values must be ignored and the next header must be consulted; if all are invalid, fall back to "http". Hidden tests that must pass: `TestContext_Scheme`, `TestContext_Scheme/ignores_invalid_X-Forwarded-Proto_and_uses_X-Forwarded-Protocol`, `TestContext_Scheme/ignores_invalid_forwarded_headers_and_falls_back_to_http`.

Apply this replacement for the Scheme method (keep the surrounding doc comment):

func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}

BUT with validity checks: a header value is only accepted when it is exactly "http" or "https" (case-insensitive comparison is fine, return the original value). Concretely write it as:

func (c *context) Scheme() string {
	// Can't use `r.Request.URL.Scheme`
	// See: https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/golang-nuts/pMUkBlQBDF0
	if c.IsTLS() {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProtocol); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	if ssl := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedSsl); ssl == "on" {
		return "https"
	}
	if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXUrlScheme); scheme != "" {
		return scheme
	}
	return "http"
}

IMPORTANT: the above is the CURRENT buggy code. Change each of the four `scheme != ""` conditions into a validity check using a new unexported helper you add to context.go:

func isValidScheme(scheme string) bool {
	return strings.EqualFold(scheme, "http") || strings.EqualFold(scheme, "https")
}

so the conditions become `if scheme := c.request.Header.Get(HeaderXForwardedProto); isValidScheme(scheme) { return scheme }` etc. (X-Forwarded-Ssl keeps its `ssl == "on"` check). Add `strings` to the import block if not present (check with grep).

VERIFY: `cd /echo && gofmt -l context.go && go build ./... && go vet . && go test -run 'TestContext' -v . 2>&1 | tail -40` and `cd /echo && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -30`. Also write a TEMPORARY test /echo/zz_scheme_tmp_test.go (package echo) with a test TestZZSchemeTmp covering: (a) X-Forwarded-Proto=invalid + X-Forwarded-Protocol=https -> "https"; (b) all four headers invalid -> "http"; (c) X-Forwarded-Proto=https -> "https"; (d) X-Forwarded-Ssl=on -> "https"; (e) X-Url-Scheme=https -> "https"; (f) TLS -> "https". Run it, report output, then DELETE the temp file and confirm `git status --porcelain` shows only context.go modified. Report the diff and all outputs.

Fix a bug in /echo/bind.go (Go, labstack/echo). Only edit /echo/bind.go; never modify existing *_test.go files (temporary test files must be deleted before you finish).

BUG: in `func (b *DefaultBinder) bindData(destination interface{}, data map[string][]string, tag string) error` the map branch is:

	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		for k, v := range data {
			val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
		}
		return nil
	}

This only works for maps whose element type is string; for `map[string][]string` it panics or binds wrongly. Hidden tests that must pass: `TestDefaultBinder_bindDataToMap` and its subtest `TestDefaultBinder_bindDataToMap/ok,_bind_to_map[string][]string`.

FIX: replace the map branch with a kind-aware implementation that supports map[string]string (first value), map[string][]string (whole slice), map[string]int, map[string]int64, map[string]bool, map[string]float64 and map[string]interface{} (first value), and returns an error for unsupported element kinds. Use this code:

	// Map
	if typ.Kind() == reflect.Map {
		k := typ.Elem().Kind()
		isElemInterface := k == reflect.Interface
		isElemString := k == reflect.String
		isElemSlice := k == reflect.Slice
		isElemInt := k == reflect.Int
		isElemInt64 := k == reflect.Int64
		isElemBool := k == reflect.Bool
		isElemFloat := k == reflect.Float64

		if !(isElemSlice || isElemString || isElemInt || isElemBool || isElemFloat || isElemInterface || isElemInt64) {
			return errors.New("binding element must be a map[string][]string, map[string]string, map[string]int, map[string]int64, map[string]bool, map[string]float64 or map[string]interface{}")
		}

		for k, v := range data {
			if isElemString {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
			} else if isElemSlice {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v))
			} else if isElemInt {
				n, err := strconv.Atoi(v[0])
				if err != nil {
					return errors.New("failed to bind field value to map[string]int")
				}
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(n))
			} else if isElemInt64 {
				n, err := strconv.ParseInt(v[0], 10, 64)
				if err != nil {
					return errors.New("failed to bind field value to map[string]int64")
				}
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(n))
			} else if isElemBool {
				b, err := strconv.ParseBool(v[0])
				if err != nil {
					return errors.New("failed to bind field value to map[string]bool")
				}
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(b))
			} else if isElemFloat {
				f, err := strconv.ParseFloat(v[0], 64)
				if err != nil {
					return errors.New("failed to bind field value to map[string]float64")
				}
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(f))
			} else if isElemInterface {
				val.SetMapIndex(reflect.ValueOf(k), reflect.ValueOf(v[0]))
			}
		}
		return nil
	}

Keep imports tidy (strconv, errors, reflect already imported - verify with grep).

VERIFY: `cd /echo && gofmt -l bind.go && go build ./... && go test -run 'TestDefaultBinder|TestBind' -v . 2>&1 | tail -60` and `cd /echo && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -30`. Then write a TEMPORARY test /echo/zz_bindmap_tmp_test.go (package echo) TestZZBindMapTmp that calls `(&DefaultBinder{}).bindData(&map[string][]string{}, map[string][]string{"foo": {"bar", "baz"}}, "query")` and asserts result is map[string][]string{"foo": {"bar","baz"}}, plus map[string]string{"foo":"bar"}, map[string]int{"foo":1}, map[string]bool{"foo":true}, map[string]interface{}{"foo":"bar"} cases. Run it, report output, then DELETE the temp file and confirm `git status --porcelain` shows only bind.go modified. Report diff and all outputs.
